# NOTE for anyone comparing this with the python sibling's .dockerignore, which excludes
# local_identity.py so that DIAGRID_QUICKSTART_IDENTITY=local cannot work in a container: that
# guard is NOT here, and its absence is deliberate rather than an oversight. A C# source file is
# compiled into the assembly and cannot be dropped from an image, so the same fail-closed
# behaviour is enforced at compile time instead -- LocalIdentity.cs is behind `#if DEBUG`, the
# Dockerfile publishes `-c Release`, and Program.cs's Release branch throws at start-up when the
# variable is set. Different mechanism, same effect: setting it on a container refuses to start.
